<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?>
<catalogue library="true" id="577a-2f18-0d58-7a37" name="Xenos - T&apos;au Empire" gameSystemId="sys-ddf1-f1c4-f4c4-87c4" gameSystemRevision="1" revision="1" battleScribeVersion="2.03" type="catalogue" xmlns="http://www.battlescribe.net/schema/catalogueSchema">
  <sharedRules>
    <rule name="Coordinated Fire" id="259f-b137-ceea-ef6c" hidden="false">
      <description>A formation that contains at least one unit with Coordinated Fire can order up to two other un-broken formations within 15cm that have not taken an action this turn to follow their own formation when they take an Advance, Double or Sustained Fire action.


Make a single Initiative roll for all foarmations, counting a single -1 modifier if any have Blast Markers. If the test is failed then the original formation (containing the unit calling for Coordinated Fire) receives a Blast Marker and must take a hold action. The other formations are unaffected (and may take an action later in the turn). If the test is passed then all formations concerned are allowed to take either an Advance, Double or Sustained Fire action.


There is no obligation for all formations to take the same action, and these actions may be resolved in any order, but they must all fire at the same target formation. If the formation being activated is unable or unwilling to fire at the selected formation, it cannot fire at all that turn. The formations don’t have to stay within a given distance of each other and will complete their actions one after the other. Each formations action is declared and resolved (including testing to see if the target formation breaks) before moving on to the next Tau formation.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Guided Missiles" id="d0c3-bc52-f624-caa0" hidden="false">
      <alias>GM</alias>
      <alias>Guided</alias>
      <description>Guided Missiles may be fired without Line of Sight, but may only be fired at a targets that are Marked with Markerlights.


Guided Missiles follow all the normal suppression rules. If a unit with a Guided Missile weapon is within range and Line of Sight to a unit in the target formation then it is counted for suppression purposes, even if the target formation is not Marked.


Guided Missiles counts as having Line of Sight to all units in a Marked formation for the purpose of suppression, Crossfire and when shooting as part of an Overwatch action.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Markerlights" id="0b46-991e-b923-64fd" hidden="false">
      <alias>Markerlight</alias>
      <description>All enemy formations with at least one unit within 30cm range and Line of Sight of at least one Tau unit with the Markerlights special rule is considered to be Marked. When shooting at a Marked formation, all ranged firepower attacks gain an additional +1 modifier to their To-Hit roll. 


This bonus for shooting at a Marked enemy may not be used when making Anti-Aircraft attacks, or with BP type attacks. A Tau formation that is broken or has Marched this turn may not mark enemy formations.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Tau Jet Packs" id="1b68-c82d-a0d9-8527" hidden="false">
      <description>Tau Jet Packs follow all the rules for Jump Packs. In addition, formations that exclusively consists of units with Tau Jet Packs are allowed to make an extra move of up to 10cm at the end of an Advance, Double or March action. The extra move is allowed whether or not the unit fires and takes place after any firing. This extra move may be in any direction and follows all the normal movement rules, so unit coherency and zones of control must be adhered to as usual.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Deflector Shield" id="445f-b7fc-a799-9480" hidden="false">
      <description>Tau Deflector Shields work like an Invulnerable Save in all respects, except it is 5+ instead of 6+</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Strategy Rating and Initiative" id="db68-b239-1360-75f4" hidden="false">
      <description>Tau armies have a Strategy Rating of 3. XV8 Crisis Battlesuit, XV10 Heavy Battlesuit Cadres, KV128 Stormsurge, and KX139 Supremacy Armour have an Initiative Rating of 1+. All other formations have an Initiative Rating of 2+. </description>
      <comment>vior&apos;la</comment>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Ethereal" id="26d0-7bed-ad25-c887" hidden="false">
      <description>All units in a formation joined by an Ethereal gain Fearless. When the unit with the Ethereal is killed the formation loses Fearless and receives 1D3 Blast Markers.</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
